  "summary": "I wrote the endless runner in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it in a browser or run `vite build`, so it is untested at runtime.\n\n- **Gameplay:**\n  - The runner stays at the origin while the track dashes and trees scroll past.\n  - Space, ArrowUp, W or a pointer click jumps. A jump only starts from the ground, and it follows a gravity arc.\n  - Hurdles come from a seeded random generator, with heights 0.4–1.0 m and gaps that grow with speed.\n  - Hitting a hurdle sets `lost`.\n  - Speed rises from 8 m/s by 0.02 m/s per meter.\n  - Reaching 500 m sets `won`.\n- **Start and restart:**\n  - The game starts in `ready` and begins on the first jump input.\n  - R resets to `ready` at 0 m.\n  - A jump input after `lost` or `won` resets and starts running at once. The task didn't say which of these two restarts should land in, so I chose.\n- **Seed:** The seed defaults to 20240607 and can be set with `?seed=`. It is the same on every restart, so a seed always gives the same hurdle layout.\n- **HUD:** A DOM bar below the canvas shows distance, best distance for the session and status. A DOM overlay covers the canvas on `ready`, `lost` and `won` with a restart hint.\n- **State and readiness:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame with `status`, `score`, `speed` and `airborne`. `window.__TASK_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n\n",
